                <pb facs="0674" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-02T13:00:00-05:00">April 2, 1929—1
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Referring to telegram No. 30, April 1, 9 p.m. from Legation at Tegucigalpa.
                    The Department is replying as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows substance of telegram No. 26, April 2, 1 p.m., to the Minister in
                    Honduras printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Please inform the Department at once whether there has been any friction along
                    the frontier which would afford a basis for the statements of the Honduran
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
